license: Apache-2.0

abstract: >
  Lean 4 formalization of the Interpretive Kernel of Structural
  Explainability. The theory investigates how equivalence relations
  on distinct carriers are related through explicit interpretations
  and selected probes. It defines the interpretation-induced kernel and
  its left adjoint, the generated occurrence regime, and establishes the
  adjunction, preservation laws, probe-family laws, interpretive
  thresholds, and a generalized-ultrametric representation of the kernel,
  together with finite witnesses of incompatibility and finite
  counterexamples. The theory characterizes the mathematical conditions
  under which interpretations preserve or distinguish declared
  relationships without presupposing agreement about domain meaning.

keywords:
